{
 "_readme": [
  "MALL OPENINGS TRACKER — how many new stores open at the top US malls we follow, and how many of them are China-origin chains.",
  "",
  "METHOD SINCE 24 NOV 2026 (owner's design): SNAPSHOT COMPARISON. On a start date we record every store a mall lists",
  "(the BASELINE). We re-read the directory periodically and compare the newest list with the baseline: a store trading",
  "now that was not trading at the baseline is a NEW OPENING in that window; one trading at the baseline and gone now is",
  "a closure. Each opening is marked China-origin by an exact name match to the register's chains (overridable in",
  "`tenant_overrides`). Snapshots live in manual/mall_snapshots/<mall-id>/<date>.json and are never edited.",
  "Capture: `python -m chain_atlas mall-snapshot` reads every mall whose row has a `directory` reader (Westfield so far).",
  "Malls without a scripted reader need a hand capture into the same file format; until then they have no baseline and",
  "are left out of the comparison. Code: chain_atlas/mall_snapshots.py.",
  "",
  "Universe is '25 of the top US malls' (by size/prominence) — NOT 'all US malls'. Top malls skew premium/Asian-metro, so",
  "the China-origin share runs higher than an all-US-mall average; label it precisely. Pop-ups are not openings.",
  "",
  "LEGACY (`sweeps`): the earlier method captured only tenants a mall TAGGED 'New' / 'Coming Soon' on the sweep date.",
  "It has no defined time frame (each mall decides how long a store stays tagged), so it is no longer the headline; it is",
  "published as `tagged`, dated, only until the first snapshot comparison exists. 'complete': true = the sweep captured",
  "the mall's full tagged set."
 ],
